<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">On the Origin of Species</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">On the Origin of Species is the book by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin">Charles Darwin</a>, published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in November 1859, that set out the theory of evolution by natural selection. Arguing from extensive evidence that species descend with modification from common ancestors, it transformed biology and provoked a wide debate about humanity's place in nature and about religious belief.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/on-the-origin-of-species.jpg" alt="On the Origin of Species" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Murray, Publisher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Origin_of_Species_title_page.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
